21f0bff28a69d4e67c79e05141532"},"arguments":{},"freshPromptText":"User requests SQL Server container-based guideline for huge whole-table counts with the same practical, no-service-degradation priorities as existing MySQL work. Read AGENTS.md, docs\/table-count-guideline.md and calibration. You are GPT-6.1 Sol author\/implementer, separate from reviewers. Do NOT start Docker\/DB\/measurement, delegate, run workflows, commit\/push. You may inspect files and official Microsoft docs and run local syntax checks only. Owner handles actual container runs. Implement NOW, not just plan.\nCreate sqlserver\/compose.yaml and sqlserver\/lab.rb (Ruby4.0.9 controller, standard library, docker exec sqlcmd only; no external DB connections\/host\/DSN overrides), regeneration SQL as needed, docs\/sqlserver-table-count-guideline.md Japanese, results\/sqlserver\/plan.json. Add a distinct mise task sqlserver-all; do not alter MySQL all, sources or old docs\/proofs. New AGENTS SQL Server override governs. Container name lab-sqlserver-count; image mcr.microsoft.com\/mssql\/server:2025-latest@sha256:245f6b1c8903edae52cb20fa31419cefcde1a49938bb8c3447099011fc871ca3 linux\/amd64 (actual tested boot 17.0.5035.5 SQL2025CU10 Ubuntu24.04.5). Developer EULA accepted local lab; fixed public lab-only credential CountLab_Only_2026!. ARM64 Docker host is emulated, Microsoft unsupported; absolute\/native performance unmeasured. 8GB Docker RAM; use4GB limit\/3GBSQL memory,2CPU, no host exposed port, own named volume. Do not touch other Docker containers. Owner has a disposable container with that name live for feasibility only; owner removes it before canonical compose all.\nFocused essential experiments only (not exhaustive grid): fixture-known true counts vs sys.dm_db_partition_stats (index_id IN(0,1), sum all partitions, do not doublecount secondary) vs sys.partitions and optimizer statistics rows\/sys.dm_db_stats_properties, distinguishing these different mechanisms and permissions. Include empty, heap, clustered+secondary, wide80\/100 columns incl encrypted ciphertext blob, partitioned rowstore, columnstore, skew\/gaps; a100M thin table if feasible within bounded runtime\/disk and approx750k80\/100columnTDE fixture (do not pretend measured if unavailable; report notrun). Prefer few representative fixtures, not full crosses. TDE configured local certificate\/masterkey only in generated container (never commit secrets\/key\/tabledata). Wait encryption_state=3 with bounded deadline, record server capability, plaintext client does not need key toCOUNT but server needs key; no server key means unavailable. Can use ciphertext varbinary fixture to demonstrate COUNT does not decode values. Logical row size\/index and memory state; no DBCC DROPCLEANBUFFERS\/global cache flush or autoUPDATESTATISTICS on service. Any ANALYZE equivalent only fixture preparation not recommended production.\nCOUNT_BIG only under preconfigured RCSI\/READ COMMITTED or SNAPSHOT in dedicated lab DB; no default locking RC count on nonversioned target, NOLOCK\/READPAST\/TABLOCK\/SERIALIZABLE or deliberate pendingDDL\/blocking injections. SQL Server always Sch-S etc; cannot promise zero locks. No global prod RCSI enable advice, configuration change belongs owner separate migration. COUNT vs stats on quiet known truth, repeated small variation to observe min\/max but no universal10% bound; metadata is not same as sampled optimizer stats, stale optimizer stats don't establish DMV error. sys.dm_db_partition_stats permissions SQL2022+ VIEW DATABASE PERFORMANCE STATE\/VIEW SECURITY DEFINITION; sys.partitions metadata visibility; RLS\/execution context can make metadata and visibleCOUNT differ—do not present tenant exactness frommetadata. COUNT_BIG avoid int overflow. Columnstore delta\/delete should be explicit if not exercised. Memoryoptimized, external, temporal\/history, views\/partition\/shards have routing or defer, no unfounded support claims.\nInclude one small honest service-impact paired baseline vs exactcount vs metadata under natural workload, using monotonic time, timed cancellation\/deadline, no excluded intentional table locks. Keep raw arrivals\/outcomes\/latencies\/unfinished and server termination check; no sparse-windowSLO pass, no client-disconnect=cleanup claim. If sophisticated impact cannot be made reliable quickly, produce narrow explicit diagnostic and retain unavailable SLO status, do not invent assurance. Capture server logicalreads\/CPU\/durations separately from docker startup\/CLI overhead, cache\/order provenance. No universal fastest\/ranking fromtinyemulatedexperiment.\nRunner must implement all=blank only ownlab volume create\/load\/measure\/integrity\/checkcleanup, failclosed on invalid artifacts\/method errors, raw failures retained, all results JSON with runid, seed, source file SHAs before\/after, actual exit status and cleanup, image digest\/id\/host arch\/version, observed min\/max signed\/absolute errors +conditions derived programmatically. Bounded time and fixture scaling explicitly recorded. Exact method budgets vs completion vs precision vs service budget vs cleanup separate. Unknown\/null\/permissions\/timeouts never0. Do not assert planned100M or encryption done. For live writes initial\/final oracle account exact committed delta or restorefixture before count. Keep size bounded (<15GB), use set-based batched generators not perrow clientloop; no huge data JSON perrow. Root may runall after code verified. Do not start database fromauthor.\nGuide should be concise (~200lines), first approvedexistingexports\/metadata (SQL canstilllock\/getmetadata, budget), then resources-isolated copy\/readablereplica correctly accounting AG readable secondary snapshot\/freshness\/redo contention and backups+TDEkey provisioning; no isolation feasible=>defer. Include safe snippets SETLOCK_TIMEOUT (notquerydeadline), sessioncontext, drivercommandtimeout and servercancel\/rollbackverify distinct, sessionID ownership notblindkill, resource